WEBVTT

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:11.812
Completed orders shows how your orders went: what came in, what it earned, and how fast the team got it out. In this video, you’ll read the numbers, filter the list, and ask Assist about it.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:17.636
Open Order Tracking, and click Completed. Pick a period, from today to all time.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:23.817
At the top: orders, revenue, the average order, how long orders take, and how many were on time.

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:28.832
Below, orders by day, the top items, and who completed them, and how fast.

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:37.203
The list has every order, newest first. Filter by location, pickup or delivery, or person, and export it to a spreadsheet.

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:44.557
Or ask Assist right on the page. What were the best sellers, and what barely sold? Which days and hours were busiest?

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:54.749
Assist answers from the orders in front of you, with the numbers behind each point, so you can act on it: drop a slow seller, or put more people on at the busy hours.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:02.411
Every number here only counts completed orders. Open ones stay on the Active board, until they’re picked up or delivered.

